<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan Pablo Duarte</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1813">1813</a>–<a href="/years/1876">1876</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan Pablo Duarte was the leading founding father of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a>. In 1838 he founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/secret-society">secret society</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-trinitaria">La Trinitaria</a> to organise resistance to Haitian rule. Independence was proclaimed on 27 February 1844 by his associates <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-del-rosario-sanchez">Francisco del Rosario Sánchez</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramon-matias-mella">Ramón Matías Mella</a>, but Duarte was soon exiled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-santana">Pedro Santana</a> and died in Venezuela.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juan-pablo-duarte.jpg" alt="Juan Pablo Duarte" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abelardo Rodríguez Urdaneta (1870-1933). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juan_pablo_duarte_diez.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
